-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Silkworm
  Publisher   Virgin Games, 1989
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Silkworm (1989)(Virgin Games)(128K).z80
  MD5         8fad50cd8c218ade32bf3c2332c8ee03

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. Game logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu,
  are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The set's own colours: green helicopter and jeep, red and orange
              enemies, coloured turrets and bubbles, the set's ground for each
              wave, the tan and red logo. Source: Enhanced colours: Ynicky
              (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: the original game on the Next, start-up only, with a
              loading screen from the same game's Mastertronic Plus tape;
              Enhanced colours from the Spec256 set, off by default: figures,
              stars and ground on Layer 2, the title's logo, the jeep's lives
              as sprites; three cheats from the archive, tested

  Note        Keys: on the title 1 to 4 pick the helicopter's controls (3
              keyboard, 4 Kempston), 5 to 8 the jeep's (7 keyboard, 8
              Kempston), 0 starts. Keyboard: O left, P right, Q up, A down,
              SPACE fire. Default: the original game, picture and pace; white
              figures on black never reach the ground, so no colour clash and
              none claimed fixed. Enhanced, off by default: the Spec256 set's
              colours as they are. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: Enhanced
              pace in JNext -2.80% to -0.47% over whole runs, slowest
              20-update stretch +1.72% in play, +15.65% once at the end of
              GAME OVER; the title's logo can blink when a control is picked.
              Missing: the archive's Immunity (no effect found) and Bullets
              (ask for a value) cheats; natural play to the end; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune jeep
   3  Immune helicopter

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

